  <section>
    <div class=3D"section-head">
      <h2>The same story, told in words</h2>
      <p>The diagrams above show the steps. Here's what actually happens to=
 Commercial Banking's request in each world.</p>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"story-grid" style=3D"margin-top:20px;">
      <div class=3D"story before">
        <span class=3D"tag">TODAY</span>
        <h3>The Word-and-email version</h3>
        <p>On a Monday morning, someone on the Commercial Banking team emai=
ls the FCRM shared inbox: <i>"We want to start banking cannabis dispensarie=
s in Colorado and Michigan =E2=80=94 can we get sign-off?"</i> A one-page w=
rite-up is attached. The email sits there for a few days until an analyst =
=E2=80=94 whoever happens to have room on their plate =E2=80=94 picks it up=
.</p>
        <p>She starts by trying to find the bank's policy on cannabis-relat=
ed businesses, and discovers three different versions of it saved in differ=
ent SharePoint folders, from different years, with no obvious way to tell w=
hich one is current. She emails a few colleagues to ask if anyone has handl=
ed a case like this before; some are out, some don't remember the details. =
Over the next several days she manually looks up every dispensary owner's n=
ame against sanctions and watch lists, one at a time, and writes up her con=
clusions in a Word document =E2=80=94 largely based on her own judgment, si=
nce there's no shared checklist that guarantees two analysts would score th=
e same case the same way.</p>
        <p>By the time her write-up is ready, ping-ponging emails with Comm=
ercial Banking to fill gaps has eaten several more days. It finally goes to=
 the Risk Committee, who see it for the first time at their next scheduled =
monthly meeting (if it misses the cutoff, it waits a full extra month). <b>=
Total elapsed time: 15 to 20 business days</b>, assuming nothing gets delay=
ed along the way =E2=80=94 and if an examiner asks about this decision eigh=
t months from now, someone has to go digging through old emails and Word dr=
afts to piece the reasoning back together.</p>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"story after">
        <span class=3D"tag">WITH THE WORKBENCH</span>
        <h3>Same case, start to finish</h3>
        <p>The same Monday morning, the Commercial Banking lead logs into t=
he Workbench and fills out a short form: what's changing (a new customer se=
gment), where (Colorado and Michigan), and who's affected. She attaches the=
 same one-page write-up. The system opens <span class=3D"mono">Case FCRM-20=
26-0142</span> immediately.</p>
        <p>Within the hour, three things happen automatically and at the sa=
me time: the system reads the attached write-up and pulls out the facts tha=
t matter; it finds the bank's <em>current</em> cannabis-banking policy (jus=
t one, unambiguous, versioned document) along with the two most similar cas=
es the bank has handled before; and it checks every named dispensary owner =
against sanctions and watch lists =E2=80=94 all of them, not just the easy =
ones. The system then applies the bank's official risk scorecard =E2=80=94 =
the same scorecard every single time, so the outcome doesn't depend on who =
happened to be on duty =E2=80=94 and writes a full draft assessment with ev=
ery fact and policy citation traceable back to its source.</p>
        <p>That same day, an FCRM analyst opens the draft, reviews it, asks=
 one quick clarifying question through the platform instead of over email, =
and finalizes it. By the next day, the Risk Committee reviews the same comp=
lete record and records its decision: <b>Approved, with conditions</b> =E2=
=80=94 dispensary clients must show current state licensing, cash deposits =
are capped per client per month, and accounts are re-screened every quarter=
. Commercial Banking is notified automatically. <b>Total elapsed time: abou=
t 2 business days.</b> Eight months later, if an examiner asks why this was=
 approved, the analyst opens the case file and has the complete answer =E2=
=80=94 every document, every citation, every decision, timestamped =E2=80=
=94 in seconds.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class=3D"section-head">
      <h2>What actually changed</h2>
      <p>Five things a bank's risk leadership, and its examiners, care abou=
t =E2=80=94 before and after.</p>
