          <tr><td class=3D"dim">Consistency</td><td class=3D"before-cell">D=
epends on which analyst picks up the case and what they happen to remember;=
 two analysts can reach different conclusions on the same facts</td><td cla=
ss=3D"after-cell">Every case runs against the same policy library and the s=
ame weighted scorecard, so the same facts produce the same rating</td></tr>
          <tr><td class=3D"dim">Completeness</td><td class=3D"before-cell">=
Watch-list checks are manual and one name at a time =E2=80=94 easy to skip =
or shortcut under time pressure</td><td class=3D"after-cell">Every named pa=
rty is screened automatically, every time, with no step skipped</td></tr>
          <tr><td class=3D"dim">Auditability</td><td class=3D"before-cell">=
Reconstructing a past decision means digging through scattered emails, Word=
 drafts and meeting notes =E2=80=94 slow and often incomplete</td><td class=
=3D"after-cell">Every fact, citation, screening result and human decision i=
s logged against the case ID, permanently and instantly retrievable</td></t=
r>
          <tr><td class=3D"dim">Human judgment</td><td class=3D"before-cell=
">One analyst's judgment carries the whole case, largely unchecked until a =
monthly committee meeting</td><td class=3D"after-cell">The system drafts an=
d cites; a human still finalizes at Gate&nbsp;1 and a human still decides a=
t Gate&nbsp;2 =E2=80=94 nothing approves itself</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

